course: dictionary
lesson: 10121
title: Thou: an old word for you
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Thou is an old word for «you». Long ago it was used for one person, as the subject of a sentence: «Thou art» means «you are». Thou goes with old verb forms that end in -st or -t, such as thou art, thou hast and thou shalt.
explain: Thou has partners: thee, thy and thine are other old forms. You will see them in the King James Bible, old hymns, Shakespeare, poems and fairy tales. When you meet them, the old-fashioned words tell you the language is old, and sometimes holy.
explain: Context clues help. In the Lord's Prayer, «Our Father, which art in heaven» uses art, an old form of are, and the prayer is about God, so you can work out that thou belongs to old and holy language. Check your guess by swapping in the modern word: «Our Father, which are in heaven» shows the same meaning, just in today's English.
fact: Thou is an old word for «you», used for one person.
fact: Thou is used with old verb forms like «thou art» (you are), «thou hast» (you have) and «thou shalt» (you shall).
fact: Thou is still used in old prayers and hymns to speak to God, as in the Lord's Prayer.
fact: «Holier than thou» is a phrase for someone who acts as if they are morally better than other people.
fact: Informally, «thou» can also mean a thousand, used by some adults about money.
exercise: In «Thou art my friend», what does thou mean? | *You, speaking to one person | The sky above | A church bell | A thousand friends
exercise: What does the phrase «holier than thou» describe? | Someone who lives near a church | Someone who sings loudly | *Someone who acts as if they are better than others | Someone who prays every day
exercise: A builder says the job cost «five thou». What does thou mean here? | A knight | A hundred | *A thousand | An old prayer
test: Which modern word replaces the old «thou art»? | they are | we are | *you are | I am
test: Which old word can mean a thousand in informal talk? | *thou | art | thy | thine
exam: In old prayers and hymns, why do writers use words like thou? | *To show the language is old and holy | To make the prayer shorter | Because modern English has no word for you | Because thou means a thousand in every sentence
